                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2155dac9-9a45-30e6-bb1d-5105ffe9cc01",
                        "entry_id": "ada14cb4-2d70-3bc8-ace4-668ff1242d83",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to the primate superfamily Lemuroidea (lemurs)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3da98035-3a26-473d-ad19-14110e845548",
                                "sense_id": "2155dac9-9a45-30e6-bb1d-5105ffe9cc01",
                                "text": "A few recent discoveries, however, expand the temporal range of both lemuroid and lorisoid primates back to the early Tertiary."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c17a478-13b9-45bd-b87b-14f3afa4d955",
                                "sense_id": "2155dac9-9a45-30e6-bb1d-5105ffe9cc01",
                                "text": "The lemuroid dentition is also closely similar to that of the greater glider in having a greater number of cutting edges on the upper molars compared with the common ringtail."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f02f0e09-db69-463a-81bf-9d52d68bc16b",
                                "sense_id": "2155dac9-9a45-30e6-bb1d-5105ffe9cc01",
                                "text": "1. In the Paleocene we find remains of small animals intermediate between the tree-shrews and the lemurs, and at the end of the Paleocene the first true Primates, small lemuroid forms."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a7f90d22-9588-384b-b66f-a81e40c7fb56",
                        "entry_id": "ada14cb4-2d70-3bc8-ace4-668ff1242d83",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a lemur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
